From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:02:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Add a setup switch for the Intel display
 audio

The HD Audio controller at 0:3.0 carries the audio of the digital
display ports of the iGPU. On the W541 those are the mini DisplayPort
and a port of the dock, DP-B and DP-C in the VBT (DisplayPort++); the
panel (eDP on DDI D) and the VGA port have no audio. Under macOS
AppleHDAHDMI_DPDriver powers that codec at every wake, and at sleep
with the display already off, and waits 10 s for an answer each time:
the wake takes 10-20 s instead of about 1.3 s, and the battery polling
of SMCBatteryManager waits with it.

Add Hardware > Graphics > "Intel display audio", on by default as the
OEM firmware has it. Off, the mainboard marks 0:3.0 disabled before
enumeration and disable_devices() of the northbridge clears DEVEN.D3EN,
at boot and at S3 resume: no OS sees the controller, nor has audio over
those two ports. The HDAU device of the DSDT stays, as an _ADR with no
function behind it.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init; the
option and its text are in the ramstage.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c       | 13 +++++++++++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index e080dc0a03..71e5ac511f 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -545,6 +545,18 @@ static const struct sm_object thunderbolt = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
+/* The HD Audio controller for the digital display ports of the iGPU, 0:3.0 */
+static const struct sm_object minihd_audio = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "minihd_audio",
+	.ui_name	= "Intel display audio",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The audio controller of the display ports of the Intel GPU:\n"
+			  "the audio over the mini DisplayPort and a port of the dock.\n"
+			  "Disabled: the controller is hidden, with that audio, and an\n"
+			  "OS does not wait for its codec at every wake (macOS).",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
 static const struct sm_object hardware_graphics = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Graphics",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
@@ -556,6 +568,7 @@ static const struct sm_object hardware_graphics = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 		&gfx_aperture_size,
 		&gfx_fb_limit,
 		&gfx_resume_init,
+		&minihd_audio,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
index 0c55fa7177..51a3dbd5ee 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
@@ -120,6 +120,23 @@ static void mainboard_enable(struct device *dev)
 			disable_root_port(2, "ExpressCard");
 		if (!get_uint_option("thunderbolt", 1))
 			disable_root_port(4, "Thunderbolt");
+
+		/*
+		 * The Intel display audio controller, 0:3.0: the audio over the
+		 * mini DisplayPort and a port of the dock, the DP++ ports of the
+		 * iGPU (the panel and VGA have none). Off, the northbridge clears
+		 * its DEVEN bit (disable_devices()), at boot and at S3 resume: no
+		 * OS sees it.
+		 */
+		if (!get_uint_option("minihd_audio", 1)) {
+			struct device *minihd = pcidev_on_root(0x03, 0);
+
+			if (minihd && minihd->enabled) {
+				printk(BIOS_INFO, "Intel display audio: disabling %s\n",
+				       dev_path(minihd));
+				minihd->enabled = 0;
+			}
+		}
 	}
 }
 
